  "prior_scope": "# Review: 506e262f9354 public-export reconciliation\n\nTask/source: production generator `3.0.0`, SHA-256 `762a30ac71d7bb9e779a6ce0948247878740259cac499842ef991e2863f20ec5` (unchanged).\nPrototype: `1.0.0` SHA-256 `5ba9b0f993c55e589f852d8818801dae560c12c54fe2cc555989a58c42920ffd` \u2192 `1.0.1` SHA-256 `90d448ac2313e78de660bd648aa49299540997cd59d814c6811700544c3b9951`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: public files were emitted while private settings were still being generated; duplicate visible IDs could overwrite silently. The writer now precomputes the complete visible batch, rejects duplicate IDs before any public write, and emits public files in lexical ID order.\nChanged scope: task-local prototype, focused tests, README, and current task notes only; `generator.py` and the canonical Racket authority are unchanged.\nVerification: `76 passed in 6.33s`; Python compilation passed.\nPreservation: seed 1 replay proves both predecessor public challenge files remain byte-for-byte identical, answer-masked, and content-addressed.\nAdversarial surfaces: natural reverse direction/ID order and forced duplicate-ID collision both have red/green regressions.\nStatus: ready for routine maintainer review; the expansion-direction variants remain `proposed_unapproved` and are not admitted to training.\nRemaining limit: this proves the selected two-setting writer contract and one forced collision path, not uniqueness against undeclared programs or general filesystem-failure behavior.\n",
